---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="PMS Sentinel — Methodology">
  <a href="/" class="text-sm text-slate-500 hover:underline">← All cards</a>
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-2 mb-4">Methodology</h1>
  <div class="prose prose-sm max-w-none space-y-4 text-slate-700">
    <p>Each device card is a structured post-market surveillance summary for a single cleared
      device, drawn from public regulatory and adverse-event sources. It is not clinical advice
      and not a regulatory determination.</p>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Data sources</h2>
    <p>FDA MAUDE adverse-event reports (device-specific where coverage permits; product-class
      cohort otherwise), and peer-reviewed and preprint literature from PubMed, Europe PMC,
      medRxiv, and ClinicalTrials.gov. EU EUDAMED vigilance and NMPA are not yet ingested.</p>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Refresh cadence</h2>
    <p>MAUDE is pulled weekly (it has a ~4-week publishing lag); literature on a per-device
      cadence (weekly to quarterly by signal density). Each card shows a "data current as of"
      watermark.</p>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Coverage transparency</h2>
    <p>A card covers what the public record covers — no more. MAUDE is passive: under-reporting
      is well documented and the absence of events is not evidence of safety. Each card states
      its tier, event counts, and the reporting window.</p>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Parsing methods</h2>
    <p>Adverse-event narratives are normalised by an LLM into structured fields (severity, IMDRF
      problem code, AI failure mode) with a confidence score; low-confidence records are
      quarantined for review. Literature is screened for device relevance, then structured. AI
      failure-mode tallies reflect what reporters described, not established device defects.</p>
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Right of reply and corrections</h2>
    <p>Before a card is published, the named manufacturer is given a 30-day right-of-reply
      window. Responses are reproduced on the card; corrections are logged and dated.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
